# Stay Safe Online: College Student Checklist (India)

## 8 Actionable Prevention Tips

- **Verify before clicking**: Always check sender email/SMS sender ID. Hover over links to see real URL—avoid if suspicious.
- **Use strong UPI PIN**: Create unique 4-6 digit PINs per app; never use birthdate/1234. Change monthly.
- **Enable 2FA everywhere**: Activate two-factor authentication on email, UPI apps (Google Pay/PhonePe), and college portals.
- **Avoid public WiFi banking**: Never access UPI/banking on college cafe WiFi—use mobile data only.
- **Don't save card details**: In apps/websites, turn off "save payment info" to prevent auto-fraud.
- **Screenshot scams**: Save evidence (SMS/email) before deleting, note exact time and amount attempted.
- **Limit social oversharing**: Avoid posting hostel room numbers, exact schedules, or bank screenshots publicly.
- **Regular app updates**: Keep UPI apps, phone OS updated—auto-update enabled blocks 80% of exploits.

## Report Immediately
- **National Cyber Crime Portal**: cybercrime.gov.in (file FIR online)
- **Helpline**: Call 1930 (24/7 UPI fraud reporting—first 1 hour crucial!)

*Print and pin on your noticeboard!*
